{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Information Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about information systems."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "computer science "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of the theory of computers and computing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Information systems are a mixture of computer science and business."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "intranet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a computer network with controlled and limited access"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: the Internet, Intranet, and Extranet resources that combine with interconnected devices and integrate with telecommunications networks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deny "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to refuse or disagree with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Nice, I can't deny your aptitude for this job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "systems analysts"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a professional dedicated to design, analyze and put in practice information systems"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In information systems you find, first, human resources. These are the programmers, the systems analysts, and the users."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "telecommunications network "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "communication between terminals nodes, which use message, packet, or circuit switching"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Internet, Intranet, and Extranet resources that combine with interconnected devices and integrate with telecommunications networks. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob08aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb Can for Ability in Negative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">can</span> with different purposes, one of them is to express ability. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <b>can</b> in negative statements to express that someone lacks any general or specific ability. The structure of can in negative statements is very similar to that of affirmative statements. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Nice, I can't deny your aptitude for this job."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can't ignore the importance of professionals and users because they create and maintain the software and hardware. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can't ignore the fundamentals such as data either, which is the engine of information in a computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can't really say that computers are an information system entirely, but an essential part of it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<center>Subject + <b>can</b> + </b>not</b> + <b>main verb in its base form</b> + complement</center>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: </br><i>You <b>cannot work</b> in information systems.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can also use the contraction <b>\u2018can't'</b> instead of <b>\u2018cannot'.</b>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:</br><i> He<b> can't </b>manage a computer software, first you need to study. </br>He <b>can't</b> access to an intranet without authorization.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can't deny your aptitude for this job. Well, do you think developers and users are important in information systems? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can't ignore the importance of professionals and users because they create and control the software and hardware."}, {"type": "example", "content": "But you can't ignore the basis such as data which is the source of information in a computer."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Computers VS Information Systems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In computing there are many concepts that seem similar. Thus, it is important to identify and make an appropriate use of them. People usually think that <b>computers</b> and <b>information systems</b> (IS) are synonyms, but there is an important difference between the two of them. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Information Systems</b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Computers </b>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Information systems (IS) is a group of components which process, store and distribute information to enhance the management in companies.</br></br>  An efficient application of IS requires knowledge about the environment and businesses involved.</br></br>   Most information systems integrate information that computer systems can give to support any company or group procedures. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Computers are machines that provide successful ways of processing data, they are a necessary part of an information system.</br></br>   Computers demonstrate the design, operation and maintenance of complex systems as being an essential part of this.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<B>EXAMPLE:</B>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<B>EXAMPLE:</B>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>When you use information systems for registering transactions, it is necessary to understand the procedures related to buying and selling stocks.</i>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>Computers, like buses, are only one component in a complex system. To understand the transportation systems it is relevant to know about roads conditions, street stops, lanes and users' needs. </i>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about information systems and computers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a concept map with these two topics."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write inside the concept map about the importance and function of these concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your concept map with the class and discuss about more information of these topics."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about information systems and computers"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I organize information systems and computers concepts in concept maps"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify importa