e": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le01ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<b>Mike</b>: Okay Oscar, let's start the interview. Can you explain to me the concept of information systems? </br>\n<b>Oscar</b>: Yes, information systems constitute a group of systems which process, store, and distribute information to improve the management of companies. </br>\n<b>Mike</b>: Excellent! Now, I want to know. What are the main components of information systems? </br>\n<b>Oscar</b>: In information systems you find, first, human resources. These are the programmers, the systems analysts, and the users. Second, there is a hardware component, which is the machines and computer systems. There is also a software that controls hardware functionality. Finally, the Internet, Intranet, and Extranet resources that combine with interconnected devices and integrate with telecommunications networks."}, {"time": "49500", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<b>Mike</b>: Nice, I can't deny your aptitude for this job. Well, do you think developers and users are important in information systems? </br>\n<b>Oscar</b>: Hmmm, what can I say? You can't ignore the importance of professionals and users because they create and control the software and hardware. </br>\n<b>Mike</b>: Yes, of course. But you can't ignore the basis such as data which is the source of information in a computer.</br>\n<b>Oscar</b>: That's right, I can also say that you can't work without any component of a software because this affects the functioning of the system."}, {"time": "82000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<b>Mike</b>: Good advice. Now, my last question. What kind of differences do you find between computers and information systems?</br>\n<b>Oscar</b>: Information systems are a mixture of computer science and business. Computers are effective machines for processing information, while information systems use different components (among these the computer) to improve the decision making process of an organization. So, we can't really say that computers are an information system entirely, but an essential part of it, which helps us process data."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le01ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}